activities.scaffolding:
Syntax & Block Mapping:
- forever loop -> basic.forever(function () { ... });
- serial write block -> serial.writeValue(nameString, valueNumber);
- sensor call -> input.temperature();
- buffer throttling -> basic.pause(500); // 500 milliseconds = 0.5s interval

activities.teacherDoes:
Guide students through building a Shake Alert algorithm in MakeCode. Model finding the 'acceleration (mg) strength' sensor block and snapping it into an 'if-else' block inside a forever container. Point out common syntax errors: 'If you leave out the clear screen block in the else path, the screen will stay lit permanently once triggered.' Guide the class to test with a threshold of 2000 mg. Modelled Example:
basic.forever(function () {
  if (input.acceleration(Dimension.Strength) > 2000) {
    basic.show_icon(IconNames.SURPRISED)
  } else {
    basic.clear_screen()
  }
})

activities.scaffolding:
Conditional structure:
if (receivedString == "CLEAR") {
    basic.clearScreen()
} else {
    basic.showString(receivedString)
}

Sender Code Template:
input.onButtonPressed(Button.A, function() {
  basic.showIcon(IconNames.Hourglass)
  radio.sendString('PING')
})
radio.onReceivedString(function(receivedString) {
  if (receivedString == 'ACK') {
    basic.showIcon(IconNames.Yes)
  }
})

